  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 211 PM MDT TUE JUL 21 2026\nFriday looks very hot as the upper high over the Great Basin\nbuilds to maximum amplitude while an upper trough stays off the \nnorthwest coast.  High temps will reach 102 to 106 degrees in the \nTreasure Valley and southern Malheur County, with 90s in the \nmountains as high as 5000 feet.  By then most of the monsoon \nmoisture will be east of our CWA but eastern Owyhee County and \nTwin Falls County will still be in it with a slight chance of \nthunderstorms.  On Saturday, upper winds will become more westerly\nas part of the offshore trough comes inland.  This means slightly\ncooler temps although still hot, but also drier.  Hot, dry weather\nwill continue through Tuesday.",
